     * Turns one bindEquationInput target into a concrete applier, and THROWS on
     * anything it cannot drive. Silently skipping an unrecognised target is the
     * worst possible outcome: the figure renders, typing changes nothing, and
     * nothing reports it. Throwing makes verify.js catch the mistake at
     * generation time instead of the student discovering it.
